WEBVTT

00:09.493 --> 00:11.675
Welcome back to the Engine Room Records

00:11.755 --> 00:12.596
Planetarium.

00:14.998 --> 00:19.082
Following the fragmentation event, the

00:19.163 --> 00:21.185
central engine has been salvaged and

00:21.245 --> 00:24.288
transported to the Star City Orbital Ward.

00:26.810 --> 00:29.773
Diagnostics indicate a complete and permanent

00:29.933 --> 00:32.636
severing of the T-10 power conduit.

00:35.437 --> 00:38.282
Automated systems below the damage threshold

00:38.342 --> 00:42.849
have officially failed. Strict manual

00:42.909 --> 00:47.576
maintenance protocols must now be initiated to

00:47.636 --> 00:49.419
ensure system survival.

01:15.769 --> 01:21.570
Strapped down to the diagnostic bed Static and

01:21.610 --> 01:25.571
the sirens ringing in my head They towed the

01:26.011 --> 01:30.392
broken metal to the star city dock Now I'm

01:30.452 --> 01:35.753
running my life on a four hour clock The

01:35.773 --> 01:40.496
automated systems are completely dead I've got

01:40.536 --> 01:46.200
to run the heavy engine on the manual instead The

01:46.540 --> 01:51.483
T-10 conduit is severed in the dark I lost the

01:51.623 --> 01:56.045
lower thrusters but I still have the spark Lock

01:56.366 --> 02:00.708
the iron dome, keep the perimeter tight I'm

02:00.749 --> 02:05.377
learning how to fly it in the middle of the night.

02:06.038 --> 02:13.224
Star City Orbital Ward. Strapped to the table,

02:13.304 --> 02:17.505
strapped to the board I hate the heavy chair, I

02:17.525 --> 02:21.846
hate the diagnostic room But I'm pushing

02:21.906 --> 02:24.886
through the fire and I'm pushing through the

02:24.926 --> 02:28.727
gloom I've got a crew to lift me, I've got a

02:28.747 --> 02:33.848
spotter on the time A heavy metal mountain that I

02:33.868 --> 02:36.889
still have to climb In the orbital ward

02:41.240 --> 02:45.324
Every 15 minutes I've got to shift the weight

02:46.185 --> 02:50.089
Trying to keep the pressure off, trying to stay

02:50.210 --> 02:53.953
straight The freight dogs pull me up the

02:54.114 --> 02:59.679
maintenance hatch A synchronized lift, a heavy

02:59.780 --> 03:04.463
metal catch My hands are on the console, I've got

03:04.503 --> 03:09.066
the upper gear We're rewriting the protocols

03:09.206 --> 03:15.349
right out here The T-10 conduit is severed in the

03:15.390 --> 03:19.912
dark I lost the lower thrusters, but I still have

03:19.972 --> 03:23.915
the spark Lock the iron, don't keep the

03:24.035 --> 03:29.403
perimeter tight I'm learning how to fly it in the

03:29.423 --> 03:34.694
middle of the night! Star City Orbital Ward!

03:36.522 --> 03:41.384
Strapped to the table, strapped to the board I

03:41.424 --> 03:45.926
hate the heavy chair, I hate the diagnostic room

03:46.426 --> 03:50.108
But I'm pushing through the fire and I'm pushing

03:50.168 --> 03:53.929
through the gloom I've got a crew to lift me, I've

03:53.989 --> 03:58.891
got a spotter on the time A heavy metal mountain

03:58.911 --> 04:02.633
that I still have to climb in the orbital ward

04:29.095 --> 04:30.476
The connection is broken.

04:33.338 --> 04:34.959
But the hands still work.

04:38.548 --> 04:39.869
The legs are silent.

04:43.091 --> 04:49.436
But the engine still roars! Star City Orbit

04:49.456 --> 04:55.857
Award! Strapped to the table, strapped to the

04:55.997 --> 04:59.398
board I hate the heavy chair, I hate the

04:59.478 --> 05:03.719
diagnostic room But I'm pushing through the

05:03.859 --> 05:07.399
fire, and I'm pushing through the gloom I've got

05:07.460 --> 05:12.701
a crew to lift me, I've got a spotter on the time A

05:12.761 --> 05:16.802
heavy metal mountain that I still have to climb

05:16.862 --> 05:18.222
in the orbital ward

05:21.835 --> 05:22.758
Shift the weight.

05:25.584 --> 05:28.631
Watch the clock. Star City Clock.

